{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRTetPNoFP87dXLSpa6DMC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 ARR reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Call for Main Conference Papers -\",\"url\":\"https://2026.eacl.org/calls/papers/\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about EMNLP 2026 and ARR reviewer guidelines. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 ARR Process\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform. Specifically, authors will follow a two-step process: Authors submit articles to ARR, where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors; Authors commit their reviewed articles to a publication venue (e.g., EMNLP 2026), where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## ARR Reviewer Guidelines\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements. The guidelines cover important aspects such as disclosure of reviewer knowledge of author identity in the ARR review form, which contains questions about the reviewers' knowledge of author identity.\n\n## Key Review Deadlines for EMNLP 2026\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nThe ARR reviewer guidelines are available at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, which contains comprehensive guidance for reviewers participating in the review process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9d03048-500b-46c5-8a1d-0e97b262c580","uuid":"5abf362a-4b93-453b-acfc-f028820f198a","timestamp":"2026-05-13T08:55:03.471Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 ARR reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01R1RnTxcWEEMFmoRshEEUCe","content":[{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/calls/main_conference_papers/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Dates and Venues – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Call for Main Conference Papers -","url":"https://2026.eacl.org/calls/papers/"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"}]},"I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026 and ARR reviewer guidelines. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 ARR Process\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform. Specifically, authors will follow a two-step process: Authors submit articles to ARR, where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors; Authors commit their reviewed articles to a publication venue (e.g., EMNLP 2026), where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## ARR Reviewer Guidelines\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements. The guidelines cover important aspects such as disclosure of reviewer knowledge of author identity in the ARR review form, which contains questions about the reviewers' knowledge of author identity.\n\n## Key Review Deadlines for EMNLP 2026\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nThe ARR reviewer guidelines are available at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, which contains comprehensive guidance for reviewers participating in the review process."],"durationSeconds":6.914774922}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GWd7aNuk6ScUugz27zRZpL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2026 January | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2026%2FJanuary\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric:\n\n## Reviewer Scores\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n### Overall Recommendation\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe overall recommendation scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award, 2 = Resubmit next cycle (substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (paper needs to be fully redone or is not relevant to the *ACL community).\n\nThe official reviewer guidelines are available at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9d03048-500b-46c5-8a1d-0e97b262c580","uuid":"134457d0-b4be-4d79-bef1-72ebb2f21a9c","timestamp":"2026-05-13T08:55:04.053Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018ueokK9T6JrVoKzwXd8YNm","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2026 January | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2026%2FJanuary"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about the ACL Rolling Review 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric:\n\n## Reviewer Scores\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\n### Excitement\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n### Overall Recommendation\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nThe overall recommendation scale includes: 5 = Consider for Award, 2 = Resubmit next cycle (substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (paper needs to be fully redone or is not relevant to the *ACL community).\n\nThe official reviewer guidelines are available at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines."],"durationSeconds":6.998338660000001}}
